    {
      "id": "macbeth/sceneV_20.5/p@134117",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MACBETH.\nHang out our banners on the outward walls;\nThe cry is still, “They come!” Our castle’s strength\nWill laugh a siege to scorn: here let them lie\nTill famine and the ague eat them up.\nWere they not forc’d with those that should be ours,\nWe might have met them dareful, beard to beard,\nAnd beat them backward home.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
