    {
      "id": "macbeth/sceneV_20.5/p@134722",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MACBETH.\nI have almost forgot the taste of fears.\nThe time has been, my senses would have cool’d\nTo hear a night-shriek; and my fell of hair\nWould at a dismal treatise rouse and stir\nAs life were in’t. I have supp’d full with horrors;\nDireness, familiar to my slaughterous thoughts,\nCannot once start me.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
